#
# Market analysis demo configuration.
#   ./scripts/demo.sh init            creates .env from this file (mode 600) and generates section 5
#   ./scripts/demo.sh doctor --keys   checks it, including that every model id is listed by its endpoint
#
# Keep comments on their own lines, never after a value. Never commit .env.
# `./scripts/demo.sh replay` needs none of this file.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Inference endpoint: the agent's models, and Auto Ontology's
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The keys are read only by Switchyard, the model router outside the sandbox, by Auto Ontology
# under the ontology profile, and by the retrieval tools when RETRIEVER_API_KEY is empty. No
# model key ever enters the OpenShell sandbox.
#
# Hermes always asks for the route "market-research"; SWITCHYARD_ROUTES picks the template
# in infra/switchyard/routes/:
#   passthrough.nemotron         every turn goes to the efficient model; no judge
#   escalation.nemotron-gpt      the efficient model answers; a GPT judge can hand the session
#                                to a capable GPT model
#   escalation.nemotron-claude   the same with Claude models (Anthropic Messages API)
#   escalation.nemotron          the same with Nemotron models only (a Nemotron judge)
#   pinned-capable.nemotron-gpt  every turn goes to the capable GPT model; no judge
#   pinned-capable.nemotron-claude  every turn goes to the capable Claude model; no judge
# In every template a Nemotron aux model (AGENT_AUX_MODEL, thinking off) serves Hermes' auxiliary
# calls and the overload fallback. The efficient, capable and judge models a template uses must all
# differ, and the aux model must differ from the efficient one. SWITCHYARD_CONFIRMATIONS (1 or 2) is
# how many "escalate" verdicts in a row move a session to the capable model.
# After editing this section run ./scripts/demo.sh restart switchyard. It applies the section to
# Switchyard, the API, Auto Ontology and retrieval, and keeps the sandbox.
#
# Default: build.nvidia.com, with Nemotron 3 Ultra answering every turn and Nemotron 3 Super
# serving the auxiliary calls. See docs/models-and-routing.md for the routing bake-offs behind it.
INFERENCE_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
# An nvapi- key from build.nvidia.com. It also serves section 2 unless RETRIEVER_API_KEY is set.
INFERENCE_API_KEY=
SWITCHYARD_ROUTES=passthrough.nemotron
AGENT_EFFICIENT_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b
AGENT_AUX_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b
SWITCHYARD_CONFIRMATIONS=1
AUTO_ONTOLOGY_REASONING_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b
AUTO_ONTOLOGY_NON_REASONING_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b
#
# A frontier model from a provider serving it (the *-gpt and *-claude templates; build.nvidia.com
# serves none). That provider serves both the capable model and the escalation judge. Switchyard
# keys a route's models by id, so the judge needs another id than the capable model: another id the
# provider lists for the same model, or another strong model there. The *-gpt templates speak the
# Responses API (an OpenAI-compatible provider); the *-claude templates speak the Anthropic Messages
# API. An empty CAPABLE_BASE_URL means INFERENCE_BASE_URL, and an empty CAPABLE_API_KEY means
# INFERENCE_API_KEY only on that same endpoint: the inference key never goes to another host.
# SWITCHYARD_ROUTES=escalation.nemotron-gpt
# AGENT_CAPABLE_MODEL=<the frontier model's id at that provider>
# AGENT_JUDGE_MODEL=<the judge's id at that provider>
# CAPABLE_BASE_URL=https://<a provider serving the frontier model>/v1
# CAPABLE_API_KEY=<that provider's key>
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint that serves every model instead (for example a gateway serving
# Nemotron and frontier models): set INFERENCE_BASE_URL and INFERENCE_API_KEY to it, leave
# CAPABLE_BASE_URL and CAPABLE_API_KEY empty, and use the model ids it lists. doctor --keys
# checks that every id the template uses is listed. Section 2 then needs its own nvapi- key.
#
# All-Nemotron escalation on build.nvidia.com (Super answers, Ultra takes over, 3.5 Lightning
# judges and serves the auxiliary calls). It passed fewer questions than Ultra alone in the bake-off:
# SWITCHYARD_ROUTES=escalation.nemotron
# AGENT_EFFICIENT_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b
# AGENT_CAPABLE_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b
# AGENT_JUDGE_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b
# AGENT_AUX_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Retriever endpoint: document embedding and reranking (retrieval, ontology)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Separate from section 1, so section 1 can point at an endpoint without the VL reranker.
RETRIEVER_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
# Empty: INFERENCE_API_KEY. Set it when section 1 uses a key that is not an nvapi- key.
RETRIEVER_API_KEY=
RETRIEVER_EMBED_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-embed-1b
RETRIEVER_RERANK_MODEL=nvidia/llama-nemotron-rerank-vl-1b-v2
# Empty: the reranker's hosted build.nvidia.com endpoint. Otherwise a full rerank URL,
# e.g. a self-hosted NIM's http://<host>:8000/v1/ranking.
RETRIEVER_RERANK_URL=
# Changing the embed model or base URL re-embeds the corpus: ./scripts/demo.sh data reindex

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. What runs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# core is always on: UI, API, Switchyard, Phoenix and the Hermes agent in its OpenShell
# sandbox. Add any of:
#   retrieval      Milvus, the document index and retrieve_evidence
#   analytics      the market analytics tools on CPU (pandas)
#   analytics-gpu  the same tools on RAPIDS (NVIDIA GPU); never together with analytics
#   ontology       Auto Ontology, required for the structured questions; needs the
#                  vendor/auto-ontology submodule (git submodule update --init --checkout vendor/auto-ontology)
# The agent image gets the matching tools and skills; demo.sh derives them from this list.
COMPOSE_PROFILES=core,retrieval,analytics
# Kumo prediction (predict_asset_outcomes, with analytics or analytics-gpu) comes from a Kumo
# Relational service on its own GPU host (docs/kumo-service.md): its https:// URL and its key,
# sent as X-API-Key. Set both to turn it on; leave both empty to keep it off.
KUMO_RELATIONAL_URL=
KUMO_API_KEY=
# Every port but the UI's (UI_BIND_HOST, below) is published on 127.0.0.1 only. On a remote host,
# use an SSH tunnel.
UI_PORT=3100
# The host address the UI is published on. Keep 127.0.0.1 unless a link that requires sign-in,
# such as a Brev link with sign-in set in the Brev console, must reach the UI; then 0.0.0.0
# exposes the UI (and, through its /api/v1 proxy, the agent) to that network with no sign-in of
# its own. The API, tools, Switchyard and Phoenix stay on 127.0.0.1 whatever this says.
UI_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Data pack
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A directory under data/packs/. After changing DATA_PACK or DATA_PACK_PROFILE on a running stack, run
# ./scripts/demo.sh up: it rebuilds the data and recreates what reads it, the sandbox included. After
# changing only DATA_CORPORA: ./scripts/demo.sh data prepare
# synthetic-market is a fictional market made with NeMo Data Designer, the default: it builds
# anywhere with nothing to fetch. A pack of your own can read real data that is never committed,
# fetched first (below; docs/data-packs.md).
DATA_PACK=synthetic-market
# synthetic-market's scale: standard (2,000 issuers, daily bars; empty means this), interactive
# (50, fast), ci (12, minute bars), intraday (500, minute bars) or large (10,000). Empty means
# the pack's default.
DATA_PACK_PROFILE=
# Comma-separated corpus sources. Empty means the pack's defaults: sec_filings (SEC EDGAR 8-K
# filings) and market_regulations (eCFR Title 17). Only sec_filings needs SEC_USER_AGENT; without
# it, use market_regulations.
DATA_CORPORA=
# Required to download SEC EDGAR filings (SEC fair-access policy): a name and an email, for
# example: Jane Doe jane@example.com
SEC_USER_AGENT=
#
# External datasets: real data that is never committed, for packs that declare them
# (docs/data-platform.md). They live in DATA_SOURCE_DIR, outside the repository; empty means
# $HOME/market-demo-data. On a VM, point it at the large disk.
DATA_SOURCE_DIR=
# Where ./scripts/demo.sh data fetch gets each dataset: DATA_SOURCE_<ID>, the id in upper case
# with - as _. A local directory or host:/path (copied with rsync), or a URL: https://host/prefix/
# or one .tar or .tar.gz archive, s3://bucket/prefix, gs://bucket/prefix, or
# hf://datasets/<owner>/<name>@<revision>/<prefix>. Empty: verify what is already in place.
# For example, a pack whose external dataset is minute-bars reads:
# DATA_SOURCE_MINUTE_BARS=
# Credentials for those URLs, only if the source needs them. Each reaches only the fetch run.
# DATA_SOURCE_HTTP_TOKEN=
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=
# AWS_REGION=
# AWS_ENDPOINT_URL=
# A host path to a service-account JSON file (empty for a public bucket):
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=
# HF_TOKEN=
#
# ./scripts/demo.sh data generate: the synthetic-market pack's text, written by NeMo Data
# Designer with Nemotron (data/generate/README.md). Building the pack never needs these: its text
# is committed. The key defaults to INFERENCE_API_KEY only when DATA_DESIGNER_BASE_URL is
# INFERENCE_BASE_URL, or for an nvapi- key on build.nvidia.com; set it for any other endpoint.
# generate also needs SEC_USER_AGENT.
# DATA_DESIGNER_API_KEY=
# DATA_DESIGNER_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
# DATA_DESIGNER_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Internal secrets, generated by ./scripts/demo.sh init
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The API's bearer key for Hermes' Runs API inside the sandbox (at least 16 characters).
# Changing it recreates the sandbox on the next `up`.
HERMES_API_SERVER_KEY=
# The key on the sandbox's receipt callbacks to the API. Hermes only ever sees an OpenShell
# placeholder. Changing it recreates the sandbox on the next `up`.
HERMES_RECEIPT_API_KEY=
# Auto Ontology's local admin password and session secret (ontology profile).
AUTO_ONTOLOGY_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
AUTO_ONTOLOGY_AUTH_SECRET=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Optional
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Voice input: a microphone in the composer. The API sends the recording to NVIDIA Nemotron
# ASR on build.nvidia.com (nemotron-speech-streaming-en-0.6b) and returns only its transcript.
# SPEECH_API_KEY is an nvapi- key; empty uses RETRIEVER_API_KEY when RETRIEVER_BASE_URL is
# build.nvidia.com. SPEECH_CLEANUP_MODEL, a public model on build.nvidia.com, deletes fillers
# and false starts from the transcript (never adds or changes a word); empty means no cleanup.
# SPEECH_INPUT_ENABLED=true
# SPEECH_API_KEY=
# SPEECH_CLEANUP_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b
# SPEECH_INPUT_MAX_SECONDS=60
#
# How long finished jobs stay available, in seconds.
# JOB_RETENTION_SECONDS=86400
